§ `Article 37(3): confidentiality of the Commission's investigations`

-- src:626 | 3. The Commission shall ensure that all sensitive information obtained in the course of its investigations pursuant to this Article is treated confidentially in accordance with Article 78.
@ref Art 37(3) (src:626)
-- Gloss: the Commission keeps the sensitive information from its investigations confidential, as Article 78 requires. Article 78 is another part's: taken as an input (seam S-78).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission treats all sensitive information obtained in the course of its investigations pursuant to this Article confidentially in accordance with Article 78` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 37(3) the Commission has treated the sensitive information confidentially` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the Commission treats all sensitive information obtained in the course of its investigations pursuant to this Article confidentially in accordance with Article 78`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall ensure that all sensitive information obtained in the course of its investigations pursuant to this Article is treated confidentially in accordance with Article 78" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:626 | 3. The Commission shall ensure that all sensitive information obtained in the course of its investigations pursuant to this Article is treated confidentially in accordance with Article 78.
@ref Art 37(3) (src:626)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 37 party` `Art 37 act`
`Art 37(3) the duty of the Commission to treat the sensitive information confidentially` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 37 Commission`
         MUST `Art 37(3) treat the sensitive information obtained in the course of its investigations confidentially`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 37(4): corrective measures, and the Commission's power to suspend, restrict or withdraw`

-- src:627 | 4. Where the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements for its notification, it shall inform the notifying Member State accordingly and request it to take the necessary corrective measures, including the suspension or withdrawal of the notification if necessary. Where the Member State fails to take the necessary corrective measures, the Commission may, by means of an implementing act, suspend, restrict or withdraw the designation. That implementing act shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 37(4) (src:627)
-- Gloss: where the Commission finds that a notified body does not meet, or no longer meets, the requirements for its notification, it tells the notifying Member State and asks it to take the corrective measures needed, including suspension or withdrawal of the notification if necessary.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements for its notification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has informed the notifying Member State accordingly and requested it to take the necessary corrective measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 37(4) first sentence the Commission has informed the notifying Member State and requested the corrective measures` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements for its notification`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `the Commission has informed the notifying Member State accordingly and requested it to take the necessary corrective measures`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall inform the notifying Member State accordingly and request it to take the necessary corrective measures" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:627 | 4. Where the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements for its notification, it shall inform the notifying Member State accordingly and request it to take the necessary corrective measures, including the suspension or withdrawal of the notification if necessary. Where the Member State fails to take the necessary corrective measures, the Commission may, by means of an implementing act, suspend, restrict or withdraw the designation. That implementing act shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 37(4) (src:627)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 37 party` `Art 37 act`
`Art 37(4) the duty of the Commission to inform the notifying Member State and request the corrective measures` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 37 Commission`
         MUST `Art 37(4) inform the notifying Member State and request it to take the necessary corrective measures`
         HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:627 | 4. Where the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements for its notification, it shall inform the notifying Member State accordingly and request it to take the necessary corrective measures, including the suspension or withdrawal of the notification if necessary. Where the Member State fails to take the necessary corrective measures, the Commission may, by means of an implementing act, suspend, restrict or withdraw the designation. That implementing act shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 37(4) (src:627)
-- Gloss: if the Member State then fails to take the corrective measures needed, the Commission may suspend, restrict or withdraw the designation by an implementing act. A "may" gated by "where": JUST FALSE where the gate is not met, as the periods ruling's rule (b) gives (fork F-37-4, split site (ii)).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements for its notification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has informed the notifying Member State accordingly and requested it to take the necessary corrective measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member State fails to take the necessary corrective measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 37(4) second sentence the Commission may suspend, restrict or withdraw the designation by means of an implementing act` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements for its notification`
        AND `the Commission has informed the notifying Member State accordingly and requested it to take the necessary corrective measures`
        AND `the Member State fails to take the necessary corrective measures`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Member State fails to take the necessary corrective measures, the Commission may, by means of an implementing act, suspend, restrict or withdraw the designation" (a power named by "may", gated by "where": the periods ruling's rule (b))

-- src:627 | 4. Where the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet or no longer meets the requirements for its notification, it shall inform the notifying Member State accordingly and request it to take the necessary corrective measures, including the suspension or withdrawal of the notification if necessary. Where the Member State fails to take the necessary corrective measures, the Commission may, by means of an implementing act, suspend, restrict or withdraw the designation. That implementing act shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 37(4) (src:627)
-- The Article 98 procedure is another part's: its answer is taken as an input (seam S-98).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the implementing act has been adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 37(4) third sentence the implementing act has been adopted in accordance with the examination procedure` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the implementing act has been adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "That implementing act shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 38(1): the sectoral group`

-- src:630 | 1. The Commission shall ensure that, with regard to high-risk AI systems, appropriate coordination and cooperation between notified bodies active in the conformity assessment procedures pursuant to this Regulation are put in place and properly operated in the form of a sectoral group of notified bodies.
@ref Art 38(1) (src:630)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `appropriate coordination and cooperation between notified bodies active in the conformity assessment procedures pursuant to this Regulation are put in place and properly operated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are put in place and operated in the form of a sectoral group of notified bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 38(1) the Commission has ensured the coordination and cooperation between notified bodies` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `appropriate coordination and cooperation between notified bodies active in the conformity assessment procedures pursuant to this Regulation are put in place and properly operated`
        AND `they are put in place and operated in the form of a sectoral group of notified bodies`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall ensure that, with regard to high-risk AI systems, appropriate coordination and cooperation between notified bodies ... are put in place and properly operated in the form of a sectoral group of notified bodies" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:630 | 1. The Commission shall ensure that, with regard to high-risk AI systems, appropriate coordination and cooperation between notified bodies active in the conformity assessment procedures pursuant to this Regulation are put in place and properly operated in the form of a sectoral group of notified bodies.
@ref Art 38(1) (src:630)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 38 party` `Art 38 act`
`Art 38(1) the duty of the Commission to ensure the coordination and cooperation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 38 Commission`
         MUST `Art 38(1) put in place and properly operate coordination and cooperation in the form of a sectoral group`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 38(2): the bodies take part in the group`

-- src:631 | 2. Each notifying authority shall ensure that the bodies notified by it participate in the work of a group referred to in paragraph 1, directly or through designated representatives.
@ref Art 38(2) (src:631)
-- Gloss: each notifying authority makes sure the bodies it has notified take part in the group's work, themselves or through representatives they have designated.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the bodies notified by the notifying authority participate in the work of the group directly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bodies notified by the notifying authority participate in the work of the group through designated representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 38(2) the notifying authority has ensured that the bodies notified by it participate in the work of the group` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the bodies notified by the notifying authority participate in the work of the group directly`
         OR `the bodies notified by the notifying authority participate in the work of the group through designated representatives`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each notifying authority shall ensure that the bodies notified by it participate in the work of a group referred to in paragraph 1, directly or through designated representatives" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
